Provide the required creation mode for the Linux 5.10 test utility's O_TMPFILE.

Ubuntu 24.04's fortified libc rejects this two-argument open() call even
though the freezer suite does not exercise the shared page-cache helper.
Use a private temporary-file mode and keep FORTIFY enabled.
---
diff --git a/tools/testing/selftests/cgroup/cgroup_util.c b/tools/testing/selftests/cgroup/cgroup_util.c
--- a/tools/testing/selftests/cgroup/cgroup_util.c
+++ b/tools/testing/selftests/cgroup/cgroup_util.c
@@ -454,4 +454,4 @@
 int get_temp_fd(void)
 {
-	return open(".", O_TMPFILE | O_RDWR | O_EXCL);
+	return open(".", O_TMPFILE | O_RDWR | O_EXCL, 0600);
 }
